s, as well as offers consumer financing in connection with the sale of VOIs; and property management services at resorts; and This segment also experiences under hospitality and leisure brands, including Club Wyndham, WorldMark, Margaritaville Vacation Club, Sports Illustrated Resorts, Eddie Bauer Adventure Club, And Accor Vacation Club. The Travel and Membership segment operates various travel businesses, including vacation exchange brands, travel technology platforms, travel memberships, and direct-to-consumer rentals. This segment also offers business-to-business private-label travel club solutions and facilitates bookings. Travel + Leisure Co. has a strategic alliance with Hornblower Group, Inc. The company was formerly known as Wyndham Destinations, Inc. and changed its name to Travel + Leisure Co. in February 2021. Travel + Leisure Co. was founded in 1990 and is headquartered in Orlando, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael D. Brown | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $212K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $28K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 24\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Travel   Leisure Co. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.5B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $523M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.78\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $17.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-17421882.42},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 28% margin of safety against estimated fair value","18 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Earnings And Awards Will Impact Travel + Leisure Stock (TNL)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-tnl/travel-leisure/news/how-earnings-and-awards-will-impact-travel-leisure-stock-tnl","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793982573.993,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.953,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Travel + Leisure Co. (NYSE:TNL) Stock to Pay Quarterly Dividend of $0.60","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/travel-leisure-co-nysetnl-stock-to-pay-quarterly-dividend-of-0-60.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793888572.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Zacks Research Upgrades Travel + Leisure (NYSE:TNL) to \u201cHold\u201d","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/zacks-research-upgrades-travel-leisure-nysetnl-to-hold.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793879291.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Travel+Leisure declares $0.60 dividend (NYSE:TNL)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666087-travel-leisure-declares-0_60-dividend","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793847334.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Travel + Leisure Co. (TNL) is a Great Momentum Stock: Should You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.